But if the AI subtly hallucinates or, say, it misinterprets a critical risk factor, reversing the entire thrust of the financial advice, the watermark will still proudly declare the document is verified.

111
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:51,940
Because it's still pointing to the hospital it was born in.

112
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:55,040
Exactly. We are completely conflating the container with the payload.

113
00:06:55,380 --> 00:07:01,780
What's fascinating to me is that other industries actually solved this exact conceptual problem decades ago.

114
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:05,480
What's fascinating here is how often tech forgets the past.

115
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:05,880
Yeah.

116
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:08,580
The paper mentions legal sotation systems, actually.

117
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:11,860
Right. Which immediately brings to mind things like shepherdizing a legal case.

118
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:19,100
Like, lawyers don't just point to an old physical case book and say, look, this piece of paper physically exists, therefore I win the argument.

